    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="1269" n="1111" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1111"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring your telegram 30th November, Treasury Department states merchandise may
                    now be shipped duty free through United States from port to port in Mexico under
                    section 3005, Revised Statutes, as amended by act of May 21, 1900, and
                    regulations similar to those proposed under section 3005 for goods from port to
                    port in United States through Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
